l":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls/72896","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/72896","diff_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/72896.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/72896.patch","merged_at":"2026-09-23T17:37:34Z"},"body":"Adds a reparse action next to each file in the Dag import errors modal, so a file that failed to parse can be retried in place, instead of waiting for the next scheduled parse or reparsing the file from elsewhere after fixing it.\n\nA file with an import error has no registered Dag, so the reparse endpoint had no per-Dag key to authorize the request against and returned `404`. Reparsing an errored file is now gated on the dedicated `REPARSE_ALL` permission (admin-by-default, scoped to the file's team via its bundle) added in #73274 — a write permission of its own, so being able to *view* import errors does not grant the reparse *action*. `ImportErrorResponse` exposes the `file_token` the button needs to call the existing reparse endpoint.\n\ncloses: #72038\n\nrelated: #72039 — an earlier, still-open draft for the same issue.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nReparse button in the import errors modal:\n\n![Reparse button in the Dag import errors modal](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/astronomer/airflow/pr-72896-screenshots/reparse-button.png)\n\nTooltip on hover:\n\n![Reparse Dag tooltip](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/astronomer/airflow/pr-72896-screenshots/reparse-button-tooltip.png)\n\n---\n\n##### Was generative AI tooling used to co-author this PR?\n\n- [X] Yes — Claude Code (Opus 4.8)\n\nGenerated-by: Claude Code (Opus 4.8) following [the guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/72896/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/